Stage 3: SELECT PLAYER "OK" -> save the player profile + set CURRENT PLAYER, then return to the menu.

Clicking OK (not CANCEL) in the SELECT PLAYER .FPL list dialog runs the player-profile SAVE tail.
asm-verified vs re_out/fist_dat_image.bin at the state-0xe handler 0xe97c (dispatched by e714's jumptable):
    e98b: call cb74                 ; modal list dialog (enumerate .FPL + cc33)
    e98e: jae  0xe9a6               ; CF=0 (OK: cc33 set CF=(a85d>=2), so a85d<2) -> the save tail
    e990: cmp  al,4 ; jne 0xe9b3    ; (CANCEL/NEW handling -- not covered by this flow)
    e9a6: call e9bd                 ; copy the selected 8.3 name -> CURRENT PLAYER, set [0x6dad]=1
    e9a9: lcall $0xf69,$0x6a9c      ; open+read(0xe6)+checksum the .FPL   (FUN_1000_612c)
    e9ae: lcall $0xf69,$0x6ade      ; create+write(0xe6) the .FPL         (FUN_1000_616e)  <- REAL write
    e9b3: jmp  0xe714               ; -> menu-idle (b78e=10)

Three faithful reconstructions (all asm-verified):
 (1) FUN_0000_e9bd -- the CURRENT-PLAYER name copy.  asm reads DGROUP:0x77bc (the 8.3 name cb74 copied
     into the caller's di=0x77bc buffer on OK) and writes ES:0xbf1 where ES=STRSEG=word[DGROUP:0x70]
     (up to 8 chars, stop at '.'/' ', NUL-terminate), then movb [0x6dad],1.  Ghidra DROPPED the ES=STRSEG
     base on the DESTINATION (raw host offset 0xbf1) -- rebased to STRSEG:0xbf1.  (The SOURCE was already
     correctly based as DAT_2000_37bc == DGROUP:0x77bc, and [0x6dad]=1 as DAT_2000_2dad.)
 (2) FUN_1000_612c (f69:6a9c) and (3) FUN_1000_616e (f69:6ade) -- the .FPL read/checksum and create/write.
     Both marshal INT-21h through the reg-file and set the DX slot (0xf0006) to the filename buffer via
     `puRam000f0006 = &DAT_2000_37bc/37ce` -- a HOST pointer written into a 16-bit DOS register (R_DX =
     low16(hostptr)) -> INT-21h AH=3D/3C opened garbage.  asm 0x612c/0x616e: `mov dx,0x77bc` (open/create)
     and `mov dx,0x77ce` (read/write buffer); R_DS is 0x1c00 (DGROUP).  Store the real DOS offsets 0x77bc /
     0x77ce.  (host-pointer-into-DOS-register reg-file artifact, patch-077 class; the ~10-site class noted
     in CLAUDE.md.)  FUN_1000_6199 (checksum) was already faithful (byte-stride word sum over DGROUP:0x77ce).

Dispatch wiring: the e714 state-0xe97c case (patch 137) now, on OK (a85d<2), runs e9bd + 612c + 616e before
returning b78e=10 (menu-idle).  On CANCEL (a85d>=2) it is unchanged (menu-idle, patch 143).

WRITE ISOLATION (harness, not engine): 616e is a REAL create+write of the player .FPL under FISTDATA/.
The engine keeps its faithful write behaviour; the harness isolates it -- tools/verify.sh runs the
"selplayer-ok" WRITE flow against a fresh cp -a scratch copy of armoredfist/ ($FIST_DATADIR) so the repo
is never mutated and every run starts from the pristine state.  The DOSBox reference (tools/refcapture_ok.sh)
mounts the same fresh copy.  `git status` stays clean after a full verify run.

